Radio page: a Lock link on every neighbour cell

The radio page lists the cells around the router, and the place to lock the modem to one of
them is two pages away: Modem -> QModem -> Advance Modem Settings -> Neighbor Cell, where the
PCI and channel had to be typed again. Each neighbour, in the table and in the card layout,
now has a "Lock…" link that opens that tab with the RAT, PCI and channel filled in
(qmodem patch 0012 reads ?tab=NeighborCell&rat=&pci=&arfcn=). Nothing is locked until the user
presses Lock there. A cell without a PCI or channel gets no link.

The new strings are translated in the de, it, pl, ru and zh_Hans catalogs.

Applies to: the 3ginfo feed pin, after 0006.
Upstream status: local to CleanWRT, like 0004.

